<p>Three Lebanese journalists were killed on Saturday when an Israeli airstrike hit a vehicle in southern Lebanon near Jezzine as they covered the Israel-Hezbollah war, according to their broadcasters and Lebanese officials. The dead were Al Mayadeen correspondent Fatima Ftouni, her brother and cameraman Mohammed Ftouni, and Al Manar correspondent Ali Shoeib. Several reports said the car was clearly marked as a press vehicle, and Lebanon’s government called the strike a violation of international law and a war crime. Israel’s military said it had targeted Shoeib, describing him as a Hezbollah operative working under journalistic cover, though multiple outlets said Israel did not publicly provide evidence for that claim. The killings add to growing concern about the safety of media workers and emergency responders in the conflict. Al Jazeera reported that the World Health Organization also condemned attacks on paramedics the same day.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ykitrVm6m_dhy-pFc4GeQ17NpzWnePNKA0ZGLiBlCezverwdWpph69QNbN6YOBvAV1Z7UNx5UmrXDKL8MA9D-Rqi8_DT_6zqhWywjT9PWQaU' alt='The husk of a destroyed vehicle that was used by a media crew of journalists who were killed in an Israeli strike earlier is pictured along the side of a road leading to Jezzine in southern Lebanon on March 28, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Prominent reporter: Shoeib was widely described as one of Al Manar’s best-known war correspondents, with decades of experience covering Israeli attacks on Lebanon.</li><li>Other injuries: The Times of Israel live blog said several other journalists were injured in the strike in Jezzine District.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israeli military: The military said it had deliberately targeted Ali Shoeib and accused him of operating within Hezbollah under the guise of journalism. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/israeli-strike-kills-three-journalists-south-lebanon'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Lebanese government: Information Minister Paul Morcos called the killings a violation of international law, and Lebanese authorities denounced the strike as a war crime. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/middle-east-war-violation-of-international-law-lebanon-on-3-journalists-deaths-in-israeli-strikes-11281025#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>Al Mayadeen: The broadcaster said Israel directly struck a clearly marked press car carrying its correspondent Fatima Ftouni and other journalists. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1986274/blatant-crime-israeli-strike-kills-3-journalists-in-southern-lebanon'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>World Health Organization: The WHO mourned a deadly day for paramedics, underscoring fears that emergency responders, as well as journalists, were being hit. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/28/three-journalists-killed-in-israeli-strike-on-marked-press-car-in-lebanon'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/28/three-journalists-killed-in-israeli-strike-on-marked-press-car-in-lebanon'>Three journalists killed in Israeli strike on marked press car in Lebanon</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/israeli-strike-kills-three-journalists-south-lebanon'>Israeli strike kills three journalists in south Lebanon</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/middle-east-war-violation-of-international-law-lebanon-on-3-journalists-deaths-in-israeli-strikes-11281025#publisher=newsstand'>&quot;Violation Of International Law&quot;: Lebanon On 3 Journalists&#x27; Deaths In Israeli Strikes</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/israeli-airstrike-in-southern-lebanon-kills-3-journalists-covering-the-war/article70797282.ece'>Israeli airstrike in southern Lebanon kills 3 journalists covering the war</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/video-israeli-airstrike-in-southern-leb